This project uses or includes material from:
- Goedel-Prover-V2 (https://github.com/Goedel-LM/Goedel-Prover-V2, Apache-2.0): prompt templates and the
  error-formatting routine (ported in app/lean_ai_station/leancheck.py; reference copy in
  docs/goedel_utils_reference.py) and the miniF2F dataset file data/minif2f.jsonl (and data/goedel_test.jsonl).
- miniF2F (https://github.com/openai/miniF2F, MIT) — original benchmark behind data/minif2f.jsonl.
- llama.cpp (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp, MIT) — downloaded and built by install.sh, not vendored.
- Model weights Goedel-LM/Goedel-Prover-V2-8B and Goedel-LM/Goedel-Formalizer-V2-8B (Apache-2.0), GGUF quantizations by
  mradermacher — downloaded by
  scripts/download_model.sh, not included in this repository.
- Lean 4 and Mathlib (Apache-2.0) — installed by elan / lake, not included.
- L Katta (https://github.com/raantss18/L-Katta, Apache-2.0) and Tontolo (https://github.com/raantss18/tontolo,
  Apache-2.0), by the same author: the model engine in madalean/brain/ (catalogue, classifier, router, quotas) is
  ported from L Katta's src/moteur.rs (itself ported from Tontolo), and madalean/brain/assets/seed.json (fallback
  catalogue of free models) comes from Tontolo.
- The On-Line Encyclopedia of Integer Sequences (https://oeis.org, © The OEIS Foundation Inc., CC BY-SA 4.0):
  madalean/research/demo_oeis/ is one recorded answer of the OEIS search (entries A000108, A120588, A115140, A168491,
  trimmed to number, name, terms, offset, keywords and four formulas), used by the demo mode and the tests of the
  conjecture engine. The engine queries oeis.org at run time only outside Local mode.
